import json,re
from pathlib import Path
p=Path('docs/reports/final-c/README.md');s=p.read_text();audit=json.loads(Path('docs/reports/final-c/final-audit.json').read_text());commands=json.loads(Path('docs/reports/final-c/final-commands.json').read_text());assert audit['rows']==47and audit['allFresh']and len(commands)==4
counts={}
for _,v in re.findall(r'^\| (L(?:7|8|9|10)-\d\d) \| ([^|]+) \|',s,re.M):counts[v.strip()]=counts.get(v.strip(),0)+1
assert sum(counts.values())==47and set(counts)<=set(['PASS','FAIL','P'])
s=s.replace('Final row counts and freshness verification are recorded after the final timing batch and native report refresh.',f"Final result: **47/47 reviews FRESH**, including **{counts.get('PASS',0)} PASS, {counts.get('FAIL',0)} measured FAIL, {counts.get('P',0)} P**. [Final audit](final-audit.json) verifies all47 tracker decisions FRESH, every review on the frozen game commit, all{audit['uniqueEvidenceFiles']} unique evidence files present with matching SHA256, and an empty game-source diff. The taste questions remain open; no release approval is inferred.")
a=s.index('## Native command results');b=s.index('## QA reporting correction',a)
section='## Native command results\n\nAll four required commands were executed again during final closure. The [command receipt](final-commands.json) records exact commands, elapsed times, exit codes and log hashes. L10 metadata was refreshed from matching native receipts after the last browser review.\n\n| Level | Command exit | Machine PASS / FAIL / NOT CHECKED |\n|---|---|---|\n'
for c in commands:
 r=json.loads(Path('docs/reports/fix51-verify/'+c['level']+'.json').read_text());cs={}
 for x in r['rows']:cs[x['currentStatus']]=cs.get(x['currentStatus'],0)+1
 section+=f"| {c['level']} | {c['exitCode']} | {cs.get('PASS',0)} / {cs.get('FAIL',0)} / {cs.get('NOT CHECKED',0)} |\n"
section+='\nMachine statuses remain distinct from this table: legacy browser adapters use their existing receipt roots/fingerprints and do not consume every new final-c immutable proof. Their remaining NOT CHECKED clauses are retained, and all fresh manual review metadata is visible. No acceptance adapter, threshold or measurement requirement was relaxed. Nonzero command exits are preserved.\n\n## Measurement scope and observer corrections\n\nNative campaign continuation, checkpoints and fixtures use actual production transactions with independent controls. Physical browser runs restore the named current native save; they establish real keyboard/mouse behavior from that point, rather than a physical whole-campaign prefix. Explicit protected-courier or isolated presentation fixtures are identified per row.\n\nThe omitted L8 transport transaction in the first harness, inside-bus L7 waypoint, standalone radar globals, and VFX particle-clock sampling were diagnosed as observer errors and corrected with separate receipts; they were not relabeled as game defects. The first high fight observer timed out without a terminal receipt. Valid earlier results were preserved; corrected high-only observer and every unadmitted reservation are archived in L10-12. Timing admission obeyed exclusive shared-pool preflight; known foreign native CPU activity is disclosed where present.\n\nRaw captures were deleted after each review, preserving only the frames/sheets needed by the review and their hashes. No push, deploy, merge, game-code or specification change was made.\n\n'
s=s[:a]+section+s[b:];p.write_text(s);print(counts)
